{
  "about": [
    "The Wiki's spaces as the two clients name them and choose among them, and what waits on the owner across",
    "them (docs/wiki-design.md §12.3.3–§12.3.4, mocks 31 ④ ⑤). The web reads this file in",
    "`src/web/src/lib/wikiSpace.test.ts` (`lib/wikiSpace.ts`); OrbitKit is to read it in its own tests (task I1),",
    "so the two ends hold one rule rather than two.",
    "",
    "`names`: spaces as `GET /api/wiki/spaces` lists them (id, title, repoUrlNorm) and each one's name: the last",
    "segment of its repository, its title when it has none, and — while two would be called the same — the",
    "segments before it, one at a time, until they differ.",
    "`defaults`: the list in the server's order (slug, workspaceIds, docs) and where the reader is — the workspace",
    "they came from (`workspaceId`; on a project's page, the workspace its coordinator runs in) and the slug they",
    "last looked at (`lastSlug`) — and the slug `/wiki` opens: the space bound to that workspace, else the last",
    "one looked at, else the one with the most documents written, the list's first on a tie; null with no space.",
    "`waiting`: the list (pendingOps, planWaiting) and the space on screen (`current`): `waiting` is the number",
    "waiting on the owner — the drawer's and the sidebar's Wiki row and the head's Activity badge, which",
    "Activity's amber banners add up to; `proposals` the proposals alone — Activity's first banner and Review's",
    "head; `banner` that first banner's words (null with none); `options` the picker's, one per space."
  ],
